ome decor products, furniture, household essential items, and home maintenance and utility items; patio furniture, air conditioners, fans, space heaters, toys, lawn and garden related products, outdoor items, holiday decor, gifts, and decorations products; books, stationery items, small electronic devices and accessories, clothing, sporting goods, pet products, automotive products, luggage and other general merchandise. It sells its products under the Ollie's, Ollie's Bargain Outlet, Good Stuff Cheap, Ollie's Army, Real Brands! Real Bargains, Sarasota Breeze, American Way brands. The company was formerly known as Bargain Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Ollie's Bargain Outlet Holdings, Inc. in March 2015. Ollie's Bargain Outlet Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1982 and is headquartered in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric  van der Valk | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $408K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $30K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Ollie's Bargain Outlet Holdings is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $5.6B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","The business throws off $195M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 72% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7239904044183529},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ollie's Bargain 